<ArticleLayout title="State Installation Research: Eight Official Starting Points" description="Verified licensing and authority starting points for eight states, with property-specific permit and fuel questions kept explicit." category="Research" categoryHref="/guides/" published="2026-10-07" updated="2026-10-07" readingTime="6 min read" toc={[]} sources={states.map(s=>({label:s.name+" official authority",href:s.source,verified:s.checkedOn}))}>
<p><strong>Quick answer:</strong> Start with the correct contractor credential and the permit authority for your property. Local AHJ requirements can differ. These eight research profiles verify a narrow official starting point; they are not completed state code guides or statewide installation-price benchmarks.</p>
<p>Choose your state below, then take the open questions to your installer. We have zero verified local quote records. State incentives, adopted code editions, gas/propane credentials, placement dimensions and permit fees are not established by this source set.</p>
{states.map(state=><details id={state.code.toLowerCase()}><summary>{state.name}: who to check and what to ask</summary><h2>{state.name} installation research</h2><p>{state.finding}</p><p><a href={state.source}>Official source</a> · Checked {state.checkedOn}. Scope: licensing or authority starting point only.</p><p><strong>Ask locally:</strong> {state.question}</p><ul><li>Which AHJ approves this address, and which current code edition and local amendments apply?</li><li>Who is authorized for electrical, natural-gas or propane work? What separate permits and inspections are required?</li><li>What manufacturer clearances, local setbacks, noise, flood and wind requirements apply to the proposed location?</li><li>Can the utility or propane supplier document capacity, pressure, storage and refill constraints for the exact model?</li><li>Who pays for meter work, trenching, restoration, pad, utility coordination and commissioning?</li><li>Is any incentive genuinely available for this project? Require official eligibility terms; none is assumed here.</li></ul><p><strong>Not established:</strong> statewide price, approval, safe setback, outage frequency or fuel availability for your property. Ask for written site-specific answers before signing.</p></details>)}
<h2>What a complete state guide still requires</h2><p>Before publishing a dedicated state guide, we require verified electrical and fuel-trade authorities, current code-adoption sources, representative local permit examples, utility instructions and applicable hazard guidance. Local examples must be labeled with their jurisdiction and date. A licensing link alone will not become a thin standalone state page.</p><p>Next: <a href="/installation/permits-and-local-requirements/">permit and placement checklist</a>, <a href="/planning/quotes/">compare the written scope</a> and <a href="/research/local-service/">verify local service</a>.</p>
